## Solution Code (Python 3 version using `eval()` safely)

Even though the original HackerRank problem is *Python 2 only*,  
this version works in **Python 3** using `eval`.

# Read x and k
x, k = map(int, input().split())

# Read polynomial as string
poly = input()

# Evaluate polynomial at x
# eval() will use the current value of x from our variable
result = eval(poly)

# Compare
print(result == k)          #print(result == k) Because it prints: True → if polynomial result equals k; False → otherwise
